<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 388-393: Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis by equidistant coordinate-grid interpolation (Archaeopteryx lithographica and Apatornis celer (pelvis, left lateral; Heilmann restorations after Marsh 1880))",
        "Thompson (1917) Figs. 388-393: Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis by equidistant coordinate-grid interpolation faithfully reproduces Archaeopteryx lithographica and Apatornis celer (pelvis, left lateral; Heilmann restorations after Marsh 1880) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-054-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-054-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-054-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-054-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-054-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Archaeopteryx lithographica and Apatornis celer (pelvis, left lateral; Heilmann restorations after Marsh 1880) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py> ;
    schema:about "Archaeopteryx lithographica and Apatornis celer (pelvis, left lateral; Heilmann restorations after Marsh 1880)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: any phylogenetic position for Apatornis beyond Clarke (2004)",
        "does_not_claim: that Heilmann's Fig. 393 series is drawn to one scale (it is not: centroid size is non-monotone)",
        "does_not_claim: that the interpolated pelves match any real intermediate Mesozoic bird (part B untestable here)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: segmentation of the wash drawings (Otsu, opening/closing) and the tip classification rule",
        "reconstructed_in_script: the grid phi as a thin-plate spline on automatically detected landmarks + arc-length semilandmarks (Fig. 389's grid lines are not digitised)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: the stage parameter t and the statistics t*, Procrustes distances, descriptors",
        "reported_in_source: Fig. 388 Archaeopteryx pelvis in Cartesian coordinates; Fig. 389 Apatornis pelvis in a transformed grid (p. 757)",
        "reported_in_source: a pelvis outline inscribed in each interpolated system (Figs. 391-392) and the five-form series (Fig. 393)",
        "reported_in_source: the intermediates are 'hypothetical types' / 'transitional stages' (pp. 757, 759)",
        "reported_in_source: three intermediate and equidistant coordinate systems interpolated between them (p. 759, Fig. 390)",
        "transfer_boundary: the registered claim's 'biologically real intermediate forms' goes beyond Thompson's 'hypothetical types'; tested only against Heilmann's own drawn intermediates" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py; output: docs/media/t1917_054_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png; organism: Archaeopteryx lithographica and Apatornis celer (pelvis, left lateral; Heilmann restorations after Marsh 1880); environment: python 3.12, numpy 1.26.4, scipy 1.x (pip, requirements.txt lower bound >=1.7), scikit-image >=0.19, matplotlib >=3.3, Pillow >=8.0, lean 4.35.0 (elan stable); claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Fig. 388 Archaeopteryx pelvis in Cartesian coordinates; Fig. 389 Apatornis pelvis in a transformed grid (p. 757) | three intermediate and equidistant coordinate systems interpolated between them (p. 759, Fig. 390) | a pelvis outline inscribed in each interpolated system (Figs. 391-392) and the five-form series (Fig. 393) | the intermediates are 'hypothetical types' / 'transitional stages' (pp. 757, 759); reconstructed_in_script: the grid phi as a thin-plate spline on automatically detected landmarks + arc-length semilandmarks (Fig. 389's grid lines are not digitised) | the stage parameter t and the statistics t*, Procrustes distances, descriptors | segmentation of the wash drawings (Otsu, opening/closing) and the tip classification rule; transfer_boundary: the registered claim's 'biologically real intermediate forms' goes beyond Thompson's 'hypothetical types'; tested only against Heilmann's own drawn intermediates; does_not_claim: that the interpolated pelves match any real intermediate Mesozoic bird (part B untestable here) | any phylogenetic position for Apatornis beyond Clarke (2004) | that Heilmann's Fig. 393 series is drawn to one scale (it is not: centroid size is non-monotone)]; other sources: On Growth and Form (Ch. XVII, On the Theory of Transformations, or the Comparison of Related Forms, pp. 757-759, Figs. 388-393) <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>; phenomenon_size: 58 µm (5.838e-05 m, log10=-4.234 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 58 µm to 13.1 cm): 58 µm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-bioelectric-polarity, 182 µm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-vertex-packing, 2.9 mm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength, 5.8 mm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-clock-wavefront, 1.3 cm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-morphogen-condensation, 1.6 cm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-elastic-buckling, 1.8 cm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-flux-canalization, 2.6 cm:archaeopteryx-lithographica-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02291478>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.24792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jeb.13256>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1206/0003-0090(2004)286%3C0001:MPTASO%3E2.0.CO;2> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-054-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-thompson1917-t1917-054-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-054-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-thompson1917-t1917-054-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-054-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-thompson1917-t1917-054-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-054-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-thompson1917-t1917-054-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-054-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-thompson1917-t1917-054-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-054-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-thompson1917-t1917-054-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-054-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-thompson1917-t1917-054-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-054-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-thompson1917-t1917-054-8> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "geometric-methodological — Thompson (1917) method of transformations: equidistant interpolation of coordinate grids between two known forms (Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis, Heilmann Figs. 388-393)" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 6.88e-01 .

