<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 388-393: Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis by equidistant coordinate-grid interpolation — Code-to-model traceability: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring maps E1-E7 to named functions, quotes the source passages, and names the Lean mirror; each function docstring cites its equation; the KG YAML pins lean_locus and code_locus per law. Deduction: code_locus entries in the KG YAML name functions rather than line ranges." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 388-393: Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis by equidistant coordinate-grid interpolation — Model fidelity to source: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "E2/E6 (equidistant interpolation), E4 (TPS), E5 (affine interpolation M_t) and E7 (t*) are implemented exactly as stated in the reference JSON and mirrored by 11 Lean theorems (endpoints/equidistance, similarity equivariance, no-fold, t* soundness, affine determinants). Deduction: Thompson's actual Fig. 389 grid is not digitised; phi is reconstructed from silhouette correspondences, and the no-fold condition (E1, det > 0) is proved in Lean but not checked numerically on the fitted TPS." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py L409–L425: phi fitted on consensus-frame configurations, not on Thompson's drawn grid lines; no Jacobian check <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8b77a9d17/thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L409-L425>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 388-393: Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis by equidistant coordinate-grid interpolation — Morphometric validation: 56/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Quantitative morphometrics are computed on the output and compared with the source's claim: t* vs nominal stages, Procrustes distance of the prediction vs two controls (nearest endpoint, affine interpolation), descriptors (pubis/ischium angles, pre/post acetabular ratio, centroid size). Missing: correspondence-free statistics (IoU, boundary RMSE), Pearson r between predicted and drawn coordinates, any null distribution or permutation p-value, and uncertainty from the digitisation (semilandmark density)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
