<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 388-393: Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis by equidistant coordinate-grid interpolation — MorphoEval overall 68.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1). Segments the five wash silhouettes of Fig. 393 from the SHA-256-pinned Internet Archive page scan (Otsu 139, opening, five components of 63-80 kpx), finds the acetabulum and the four process tips automatically, places 4 x 24 arc-length semilandmarks, runs GPA, fits the Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis grid as a thin-plate spline (E4) with an affine-only control (E5), and generates Thompson's equidistant stages phi_t (E2/E6). Heilmann's drawn intermediates sit at t* = 0.263 / 0.529 / 0.824 (nominal 0.25 / 0.5 / 0.75; max residual 0.074); the interpolated prediction is closer to each drawn stage (Procrustes 0.134 / 0.121 / 0.093) than the nearest endpoint (0.214 / 0.312 / 0.145) and than the affine interpolation (0.162 / 0.199 / 0.293). Centroid sizes 2190 / 2171 / 2158 / 2309 / 2325 px are not monotone (the series is not drawn to the grid's scale). Part B (\"biologically real\") is untestable: no landmark data for intermediate taxa; Dryad k1v34cf is a variable mismatch. Verdict in result.json: mixed (A supported, B untestable). Overall 68.8/100. Overall 68.8/100 (faithfulness 63.3, reproducibility 81.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8b77a9d17; environment: python 3.12, numpy 1.26.4, scipy 1.x (pip, requirements.txt lower bound >=1.7), scikit-image >=0.19, matplotlib >=3.3, Pillow >=8.0, lean 4.35.0 (elan stable). Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 74, Morphological realism / specimen match 66, Parameter expressivity 46, Morphometric validation 56, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 76. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_054_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py at 8b77a9d17, image/png, 737024 B, 1980×1210 px, artifact_sha256 88a7e3f72db8820186f7d06df39db6bdd6c04501cb3e21cd3ef86962116cdb2d (sha256 88a7e3f72db8820186f7d06df39db6bdd6c04501cb3e21cd3ef86962116cdb2d), spec_fingerprint 970a80c4a196f6e5a31934d373b23b236d1d7d84f48c848cb068165ec1804809. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 970a80c4a196f6e5a31934d373b23b236d1d7d84f48c848cb068165ec1804809; artifact_sha256: 88a7e3f72db8820186f7d06df39db6bdd6c04501cb3e21cd3ef86962116cdb2d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/apatornis_celer_holotype_synsacrum_marsh1880.jpg=28213a31e4c88718..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/archaeopteryx_lithographica_berlin_specimen_mfn.jpg=96341aed3d81b2b6..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/dryad_k1v34cf_deeming_mayr_2018_metadata.json=4f2b721ee3bec249..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/ongrowthform1917thom_p757_leaf0776_figs388-389.jpg=5214f00748cee71c..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/ongrowthform1917thom_p758_leaf0777_figs390-391.jpg=3b7d8054e6d7e995..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/ongrowthform1917thom_p759_leaf0778_fig392.jpg=17283e61fc562441..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/ongrowthform1917thom_p760_leaf0779_fig393.jpg=0e73dc9e37ed7e64..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/paper_citations.bib=6a29f62000543207..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/scout_manifest.json=6a8a3e51bdde2a4a..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/t1917_054_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_reference.json=92bc0f5512fe8f9d...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Fig. 388 Archaeopteryx pelvis in Cartesian coordinates; Fig. 389 Apatornis pelvis in a transformed grid (p. 757) | three intermediate and equidistant coordinate systems interpolated between them (p. 759, Fig. 390) | a pelvis outline inscribed in each interpolated system (Figs. 391-392) and the five-form series (Fig. 393) | the intermediates are 'hypothetical types' / 'transitional stages' (pp. 757, 759); reconstructed_in_script: the grid phi as a thin-plate spline on automatically detected landmarks + arc-length semilandmarks (Fig. 389's grid lines are not digitised) | the stage parameter t and the statistics t*, Procrustes distances, descriptors | segmentation of the wash drawings (Otsu, opening/closing) and the tip classification rule; transfer_boundary: the registered claim's 'biologically real intermediate forms' goes beyond Thompson's 'hypothetical types'; tested only against Heilmann's own drawn intermediates; does_not_claim: that the interpolated pelves match any real intermediate Mesozoic bird (part B untestable here) | any phylogenetic position for Apatornis beyond Clarke (2004) | that Heilmann's Fig. 393 series is drawn to one scale (it is not: centroid size is non-monotone)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=2.5]: Independent second assessor from a different provider",
        "open need [model_equation/model-fidelity, pressure P=2.5]: Numerical no-fold (Jacobian determinant) check of phi_t on the 9 x 8 grid at every stage, mirroring Lean interp_no_fold",
        "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=2.5]: Correspondence-free IoU and boundary RMSE, Pearson r of predicted vs drawn coordinates, shuffled-stage permutation null, KS test of residual distributions",
        "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=2.5]: Sweep semilandmark density (8..48) and TPS lambda; report stability of t* and of the prediction/endpoint ratio",
        "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=2.5]: CV segmentation of the Berlin Archaeopteryx photograph (bone vs matrix) and a larger predicted-vs-drawn figure",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different provider) — this round is builder-scored'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Parameter-regime sweep over n_semi in {8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48} and lambda in {0, 1e-3, 1e-2, 1e-1}; report t* and distance ratios per setting'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Negative/null controls: shuffled-stage permutation (all 3! pairings) and a random-correspondence null; report p-values'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Correspondence-free goodness of fit: IoU of superimposed filled outlines and symmetric boundary RMSE; Pearson r and RMSE of predicted vs drawn coordinates; KS test of per-landmark residuals vs endpoint-control residuals'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Jacobian no-fold check of the TPS grid at t = 0..1 (min det over the 9 x 8 grid)'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'Bone-vs-matrix colour segmentation of the Berlin Archaeopteryx specimen as a labelled, non-verdict CV pass; enlarge the predicted-vs-drawn panels'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 6.88e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

