<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-054-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson equidistant grid interpolation — endpoints, constant stage displacement and exact midpoint (E2/E6)" ;
    dct:description "Operational meaning of 'three intermediate and equidistant co-ordinate systems' (p. 759): stage 0 is Archaeopteryx, stage 4 is Apatornis, consecutive stages differ by the same displacement, stage 2 is the exact midpoint | Variables: a: coordinate of a point in the Archaeopteryx (Cartesian, Fig. 388) grid; b = phi(a): its image in the Apatornis grid (Fig. 389); k in 0..4: Thompson's stage (k/4); interp4: 4x the interpolated coordinate" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) On Growth and Form, Ch. XVII p. 759 and Fig. 390" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8b77a9d17/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_054.lean#L24-L57>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8b77a9d17/thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L358-L361> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def interp4 (k a b : Int) : Int := (4 - k) * a + k * b
theorem interp_endpoints_and_equidistant (k a b : Int) :
    interp4 0 a b = 4 * a ∧
    interp4 4 a b = 4 * b ∧
    interp4 (k + 1) a b - interp4 k a b = b - a ∧
    2 * interp4 2 a b = interp4 0 a b + interp4 4 a b
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "phi_t(x) = (1 - t) x + t phi(x);  with t = k/4 and 4 phi_{k/4}(a) = interp4(k, a, b) = (4 - k) a + k b:  interp4(0) = 4a,  interp4(4) = 4b,  interp4(k+1) - interp4(k) = b - a,  2 interp4(2) = interp4(0) + interp4(4)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02291478>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.24792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jeb.13256>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1206/0003-0090(2004)286%3C0001:MPTASO%3E2.0.CO;2> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "geometric-methodological — Thompson (1917) method of transformations: equidistant interpolation of coordinate grids between two known forms (Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis, Heilmann Figs. 388-393)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_243.interp4" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_243.interp_endpoints_and_equidistant" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-054-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Frame independence of the interpolated form — similarity equivariance (E2 under Procrustes superimposition)" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees that the choice of drawing scale/position (or of the Procrustes frame used to compare with Fig. 393) cannot change which intermediate form the construction predicts | Variables: c: common scale factor; d: common translation; a, b, k as above" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) Ch. XVII pp. 727-733 (transformations compared up to similarity); Gower (1975) Psychometrika 40:33-51" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8b77a9d17/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_054.lean#L60-L72>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8b77a9d17/thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L271-L288> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem interp_translate (k x y d : Int) :
    interp4 k (x + d) (y + d) = interp4 k x y + 4 * d
theorem interp_scale (k x y c : Int) :
    interp4 k (c * x) (c * y) = c * interp4 k x y
theorem interp_similarity_equivariant (k a b c d : Int) :
    interp4 k (c * a + d) (c * b + d) = c * interp4 k a b + 4 * d
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "interp4(k, c a + d, c b + d) = c interp4(k, a, b) + 4 d  for any scale c and translation d applied to both endpoint drawings" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02291478>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.24792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jeb.13256>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1206/0003-0090(2004)286%3C0001:MPTASO%3E2.0.CO;2> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "geometric-methodological — Thompson (1917) method of transformations: equidistant interpolation of coordinate grids between two known forms (Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis, Heilmann Figs. 388-393)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_243.interp_scale" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_243.interp_similarity_equivariant" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-054-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "No-fold property of interpolated grids — intermediate coordinate systems stay orientation-preserving (E1 at every stage, 1-D form)" ;
    dct:description "If both endpoint grids are unfolded along a coordinate line, every interpolated grid of Fig. 390 is unfolded too, so inscribing a pelvis in it is well-defined; the script's check_no_fold() tests the 2-D Jacobian analogue numerically | Variables: a1 < a2: two grid coordinates in order in the Archaeopteryx grid; b1 < b2: their images in order in the Apatornis grid" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) Ch. XVII p. 759 ('a complete co-ordinate diagram is drawn' from each interpolated system) and Fig. 390" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8b77a9d17/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_054.lean#L82-L105>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8b77a9d17/thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L312-L331> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem interp_no_fold (k a1 a2 b1 b2 : Int) (hk0 : 0 ≤ k) (hk4 : k ≤ 4)
    (ha : a1 < a2) (hb : b1 < b2) :
    interp4 k a1 b1 < interp4 k a2 b2
theorem interp_between (k a b : Int) (hk0 : 0 ≤ k) (hk4 : k ≤ 4) (hab : a ≤ b) :
    4 * a ≤ interp4 k a b ∧ interp4 k a b ≤ 4 * b
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "a1 < a2 and b1 < b2 and 0 <= k <= 4  =>  interp4(k, a1, b1) < interp4(k, a2, b2);  a <= b => 4a <= interp4(k, a, b) <= 4b" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02291478>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.24792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jeb.13256>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1206/0003-0090(2004)286%3C0001:MPTASO%3E2.0.CO;2> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "geometric-methodological — Thompson (1917) method of transformations: equidistant interpolation of coordinate grids between two known forms (Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis, Heilmann Figs. 388-393)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_243.interp4" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_243.interp_no_fold" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-054-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Soundness of the best-fit stage statistic t* (E7)" ;
    dct:description "Shows that the projection statistic used to test Thompson's 'equidistant' claim returns exactly the nominal stage for a perfect interpolant, so the measured residual |t* - k/4| attributes to Heilmann's drawing (or to the digitisation), not to the statistic | Variables: A = (Ax, Ay): Archaeopteryx landmark; B = (Bx, By): Apatornis landmark; D = (Dx, Dy): drawn intermediate landmark; k/4: nominal stage" ;
    dct:source "this loop (test statistic); Thompson (1917) p. 759 for the equidistance claim under test" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8b77a9d17/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_054.lean#L115-L134>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8b77a9d17/thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L363-L366> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem best_fit_stage_sound (k Ax Ay Bx By Dx Dy : Int)
    (hx : 4 * Dx = interp4 k Ax Bx) (hy : 4 * Dy = interp4 k Ay By) :
    4 * ((Dx - Ax) * (Bx - Ax) + (Dy - Ay) * (By - Ay)) =
      k * ((Bx - Ax) * (Bx - Ax) + (By - Ay) * (By - Ay))
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "4 D = interp4(k, A, B) (both coordinates)  =>  4 <D - A, B - A> = k |B - A|^2,  i.e. t* = <D - A, B - A>/|B - A|^2 = k/4" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02291478>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.24792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jeb.13256>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1206/0003-0090(2004)286%3C0001:MPTASO%3E2.0.CO;2> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "geometric-methodological — Thompson (1917) method of transformations: equidistant interpolation of coordinate grids between two known forms (Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis, Heilmann Figs. 388-393)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_243.interp4" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_243.best_fit_stage_sound" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-054-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Interpolation of Thompson's 'simple' affine transformations — determinant endpoints, shear area-preservation and scaling orientation-preservation (E5)" ;
    dct:description "Thompson's own catalogue of transformations (shear, simple strain) interpolates without ever reversing orientation; the script's affine-only control implements M_t and compares it with the thin-plate-spline grid | Variables: A = [[a11, a12],[a21, a22]]: linear part of the Archaeopteryx->Apatornis affine fit; s: shear; p, q: axis scalings; k: stage" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) Ch. XVII pp. 727-733 (shear, simple strain, oblique coordinates)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8b77a9d17/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_054.lean#L27-L35,#L143-L178>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8b77a9d17/thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L339-L355> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def interpDet (k a11 a12 a21 a22 : Int) : Int :=
  interpMat11 k a11 * interpMat22 k a22 - interpMat12 k a12 * interpMat21 k a21
theorem affine_interp_det_endpoints (a11 a12 a21 a22 : Int) :
    interpDet 0 a11 a12 a21 a22 = 16 ∧
    interpDet 4 a11 a12 a21 a22 = 16 * (a11 * a22 - a12 * a21)
theorem shear_interp_preserves_area (k s : Int) :
    interpDet k 1 s 0 1 = 16
theorem scaling_interp_orientation_preserving (k p q : Int)
    (hk0 : 0 ≤ k) (hp : 1 ≤ p) (hq : 1 ≤ q) :
    0 < interpDet k p 0 0 q
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "M_k = (4 - k) I + k A;  det M_0 = 16, det M_4 = 16 det A;  A = [[1, s],[0, 1]] => det M_k = 16 for all k;  A = diag(p, q), p, q >= 1, k >= 0 => det M_k > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02291478>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.24792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jeb.13256>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1206/0003-0090(2004)286%3C0001:MPTASO%3E2.0.CO;2> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "geometric-methodological — Thompson (1917) method of transformations: equidistant interpolation of coordinate grids between two known forms (Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis, Heilmann Figs. 388-393)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_243.interpDet" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_243.shear_interp_preserves_area" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

